---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import {evidence,admins,periods,url} from '../lib/data';
---
<Layout title="Administration comparison"><div class="eyebrow">Credit belongs to institutions and actions</div><h1>Compare records,<br/>without a league table.</h1><p class="lede">Congress writes laws and funds agencies. Presidents sign, veto and direct implementation. Agencies enforce across terms, and courts can preserve or overturn provisions. None of these roles is interchangeable.</p><div class="notice"><b>Insufficient evidence to rank presidents by suffering reduced.</b> This selected inventory is not balanced by item count, exposure, animal numbers or observation time. Trump’s two terms are separate; the second is still in progress.</div>
<div class="grid two">{admins.map((admin,i)=>{const policies=evidence.policies.filter((p:any)=>p.administrations.includes(admin));return <section class="card compare-card"><div class="eyebrow">{periods[i]}</div><h3>{admin}</h3><p class="small">Selected policies with a documented role during this administration. Follow each link for Congress, agency and court attribution.</p><ul>{policies.map((p:any)=><li><a href={url(`policies/${p.id}/`)}>{p.title}</a></li>)}</ul><p class="small"><b>Impact ranking:</b> insufficient comparable outcome evidence.</p></section>})}</div>
<section class="section"><h2>Dimensions that should stay separate</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What can be compared here</th><th>What prevents a score</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Breadth</td><td>Covered animal groups, activities and legal exceptions</td><td>A narrow policy can address severe suffering; number of statutes is not impact.</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>The harmful practice targeted, including torture, soring and painful procedures</td><td>No common validated severity scale across practices.</td></tr><tr><td>Scale</td><td>Reported animals or inspected entries in defined populations</td><td>Exclusions, repeated entries and missing denominators prevent a common total.</td></tr><tr><td>Durability</td><td>Enactment, court intervention, delay and rollback history</td><td>Duration in law differs from effective implementation.</td></tr><tr><td>Implementation</td><td>Agency actions and selected dispositions</td><td>Enforcement resources, targeting and reporting vary over time.</td></tr><tr><td>Outcomes and causality</td><td>Measured quantities with explicit limitations</td><td>No defensible national counterfactual or harmonized suffering measure.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="section"><h2>Unequal observation windows</h2><p class="prose">Earlier administrations have decades of follow-up; recent policies have months or a few years. A fiscal year starts on October 1, so transition years such as FY2021 and FY2025 span administrations. This site does not assign those annual totals to one president. A signature receives credit for enactment; later actions receive their own attribution.</p></section></Layout>
